20261102_195800 | model=nanopro | size=landscape_4_3 | count=1 | aspect=16:9 | resolution=2K | refs=20261102_195648_repaint_this_grey_block_mockup_as_a_fini.png
  A modular building kit sheet for an isometric pixel art game, on a plain flat light grey background, pieces separated with space between them, all at the same scale, in exactly the style of the reference image (same pixel size, outline, palette and shading). 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Pieces of a half-timbered house: ground floor wall segments with door and with window (stone plinth, plaster, oak beams), upper floor wall segments (jettied), corner posts, gable end triangle, terracotta roof slope pieces, ridge piece, chimney, dormer window, a wooden shutter, a hanging shop sign without text, and two complete houses assembled from the same pieces as examples. A 1.7 m tall villager stands next to the assembled houses for scale; a door is slightly taller than the villager.

--- Selección (2026-11-02) ---
Las pruebas con model=nano (Nano Banana) fueron iteración y se descartaron (fuera del repo). Lo que queda en esta carpeta es
la versión buena con model=nanopro (Nano Banana Pro, 2K). Las maquetas grises usadas como referencia (refs=ref_*.png)
salen de: python3 tools/art/escala.py --refs  -> tmp/escala_refs/ (densidad 1:1; las de E y A, ampliadas ×2).
